{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","software--1","instance--833bb1ab-1065-53cb-9c6f-bb4eac2fe12a","instance--ea69be26-6559-52d4-8479-a0e32478e751","process--1","instance--d562b69c-9a04-5f30-a5ee-3888fe0b887b","file--1","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--91e20d56-879b-539d-a54e-e7a44dcf7d46","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--f7a64c30-f474-5ee2-8e3a-451cd1449945","instance--b3bd4648-64f2-52d7-bf1f-c089a321f54d","instance--58f5da77-434d-5660-9890-5fd908f48e5c","instance--f64caa83-12dd-5204-a53f-519db6b69a9d","instance--7ddadc74-4c56-5579-bbe8-d8f9bd8d476f","instance--465c895a-15c7-553e-ba1a-16498ce7bbe9","instance--f369065a-4305-5c0b-bf28-c38cb43b263d","instance--958b80fd-829a-511c-b49f-68736d6d8cca","instance--cd899e97-05fa-565e-9719-2df32d8822a3"],"properties":[["name","Winnti Linux variant passive listener and host interaction flow"],["description","Chronicle Blog analysis of the Linux version of Winnti describing host execution behavior, rootkit-based hiding, configuration decoding, outbound communications, and a secondary inbound communication channel that allows operators to initiate a connection directly to an infected host."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Chronicle"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","medium.com"],["url","https://medium.com/chronicle-blog/winnti-more-than-just-windows-and-gates-e4f03436031a"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Execute rootkit library"],["description","The library used to hide Winnti\u2019s system activity is a copy of the open-source userland rootkit Azazel\u00b9\u2070, with minor changes. When executed, it will register symbols for multiple commonly used functions, including: open(), rmdir(), and unlink(), and modify their returns to hide the malware\u2019s operations."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.006"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Decode embedded configuration in rootkit"],["description","Distinct changes to Azazel by the Winnti developers include the addition of a function named \u2018Decrypt2\u2019, which is used to decode an embedded configuration similar to the core implant."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Hide malware network activity"],["description","Unlike standard Azazel which is configured to hide network activity based on port ranges, the Winnti-modified version keeps a list of process identifiers and network connections associated with the malware\u2019s activity."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1564"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Decode XOR-encoded strings"],["description","Strings within this sample associated with the malware\u2019s operations are encoded using a single-byte XOR encoding."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Execute core implant and decode configuration"],["description","Winnti Linux variant\u2019s core functionality is within \u2018libxselinux\u2019. Upon execution, an embedded configuration is decoded from the data section using a simple XOR cipher."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Use hard-coded command-and-control servers"],["description","Embedded in this sample\u2019s configuration three command-and-control server addresses and two additional strings we believe to be campaign designators."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1583.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Communicate over multiple protocols"],["description","Winnti malware handles outbound communications using multiple protocols including: ICMP, HTTP, as well as custom TCP and UDP protocols."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1095"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Initiate direct connection to infected host"],["description","a feature of recent versions of Winnti we came across in the Linux variant (as well as Windows) that allows the operators to initiate a connection directly to an infected host, without requiring a connection to a control server."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1219"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Send initial custom packet"],["description","This script identifies infected hosts by first sending a custom packet, immediately followed by an encoded request for host information, and then parsing the response."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1095"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Listen for second inbound request"],["description","When received by a Winnti-infected host, it will validate the received packet and listen for a second inbound request containing tasking."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1095"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Send encoded tasking request"],["description","This second request ( ) is encoded using the same method as the custom TCP protocol used for communication with command-and-control servers, which uses a four-byte XOR encoding."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1132.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Execute tasking"],["description","Before acting on the request, Winnti will validate the third DWORD contains the magic value 0xABC18CBA before executing tasking."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","When received by a Winnti-infected host, it will validate the received packet and listen for a second inbound request containing tasking."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","Before acting on the request, Winnti will validate the third DWORD contains the magic value 0xABC18CBA before executing tasking."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--905f37ff-524a-522a-8685-08b6df9b34bd","120":"instance--a0b8bf42-8310-53d9-87f0-390378638ae9","150":"instance--ffafa2fa-6430-5714-9c5e-bbf977c9819b","180":"instance--10bf0e4d-ac4d-5742-b82b-398ef2467e2a","210":"instance--f2066b53-6fa4-5efa-8f61-dc81d3df5b0e","240":"instance--fbb6b151-c9f4-5cb6-b467-c563cc0c60d3","270":"instance--451ff5e8-5cc8-5d6c-b701-da17c04936f7","30":"instance--059bc992-da53-5d4b-ac82-60cfacc08e81","300":"instance--1d241382-a8ee-554a-aa3a-04366535b315","330":"instance--8a7078e9-787d-56b2-a734-f93cd76b3dc8","60":"instance--8aab1831-f6e3-582d-8f9b-3ad920a40e35","90":"instance--192458e5-76c8-5d8c-ab54-9ed8b36ef2bd"},"id":"software","instance":"software--1","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"The library used to hide Winnti\u2019s system activity is a copy of the open-source userland rootkit Azazel\u00b9\u2070, with minor changes.","source":"https://medium.com/chronicle-blog/winnti-more-than-just-windows-and-gates-e4f03436031a","source_field":"normalized_text","source_object_id":null}]]],["display_name","Azazel"],["name","Azazel"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--543e6815-5cba-50f5-baa9-fc76c6011b28","120":"instance--56849cb2-2ee6-56c6-a67e-59602a29a0da","150":"instance--e06848fe-3a62-595b-b63b-843aa2d3998b","180":"instance--cdcfaa40-c56f-5af3-9bdb-ac4622d1f7a4","210":"instance--99749e6b-cf06-5316-873c-810ee9e68b8c","240":"instance--27b802d0-debb-5c29-bd76-8d14591e6691","270":"instance--45a90a34-c271-502e-8cd2-86108108594d","30":"instance--de851b9d-e5c3-5373-ac0b-408acc2b67c6","300":"instance--78c92aa5-dcc6-5a40-a1c4-b9e8c9cb3dea","330":"instance--e8c313c5-126d-5576-9281-e8ce2aba599a","60":"instance--849421d8-dc93-52be-bf77-b1cbf1d76e38","90":"instance--4d2f2fc5-0217-53d4-be7d-45effeb9fdee"},"id":"software","instance":"instance--833bb1ab-1065-53cb-9c6f-bb4eac2fe12a","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"The Linux version of Winnti is comprised of two files: a main backdoor (libxselinux) and a library (libxselinux.so) used to hide it\u2019s activity on an infected system.","source":"https://medium.com/chronicle-blog/winnti-more-than-just-windows-and-gates-e4f03436031a","source_field":"normalized_text","source_object_id":null}]]],["display_name","libxselinux.so"],["name","libxselinux.so"],["diagram_instance","instance--833bb1ab-1065-53cb-9c6f-bb4eac2fe12a"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ef7d9494-2264-5606-9719-07e3a5cc9395","120":"instance--ff321850-6f13-5372-b1ef-f3279fced335","150":"instance--78c7fb7e-3084-5e08-ba7f-ea68de55bf2b","180":"instance--b4de8f7f-abde-55e6-bab3-4a0d78a6719a","210":"instance--06d3c032-cfec-516f-b76c-e80131122e58","240":"instance--9a474758-3078-50e6-8ba4-420e3cbc285d","270":"instance--68ca5ca0-9f9e-57ec-948e-4e1494baf7de","30":"instance--160af123-c6fb-5fbf-9a38-928437404864","300":"instance--87199eed-ec2a-5c18-bb0c-606892bce50d","330":"instance--04498611-7b8b-50d2-a038-ccaa5e5bbe60","60":"instance--cb2c7194-bdba-5e02-a3ed-8486136e61fb","90":"instance--bcd65348-aed2-57cf-96f5-cf42ee767dce"},"id":"software","instance":"instance--ea69be26-6559-52d4-8479-a0e32478e751","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"The Linux version of Winnti is comprised of two files: a main backdoor (libxselinux) and a library (libxselinux.so) used to hide it\u2019s activity on an infected system.","source":"https://medium.com/chronicle-blog/winnti-more-than-just-windows-and-gates-e4f03436031a","source_field":"normalized_text","source_object_id":null}]]],["display_name","libxselinux.so"],["name","libxselinux.so"],["diagram_instance","instance--ea69be26-6559-52d4-8479-a0e32478e751"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4e942bfd-4264-555c-8748-7eb2e999ff13","120":"instance--f044726d-ee55-52f4-88b4-fd39ff2b8e8d","150":"instance--14187d6c-2f13-51e8-bde1-91e065756a74","180":"instance--72fbf7a0-91d0-5e9f-b83b-7f5b189a8cef","210":"instance--e1937ddc-1102-52c0-9709-5f7600aba57e","240":"instance--a15e1468-8c2f-564d-98f3-27d39b4d492e","270":"instance--7f152962-47bb-5430-9fc9-64786b99deff","30":"instance--b1dba1f2-201d-5b13-abad-98f28b800a58","300":"instance--eeb12b43-767c-5026-84e8-5841c4408405","330":"instance--b6b5fa0e-b8a7-5ff5-a7fd-083a3cc69914","60":"instance--9f8b261a-13e3-5220-85ca-393ef17dce5a","90":"instance--83e60b13-a495-5805-8247-5fcabd32f71b"},"id":"process","instance":"process--1","properties":[["command_line","Decrypt2"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"Distinct changes to Azazel by the Winnti developers include the addition of a function named \u2018Decrypt2\u2019, which is used to decode an embedded configuration similar to the core implant.","source":"https://medium.com/chronicle-blog/winnti-more-than-just-windows-and-gates-e4f03436031a","source_field":"normalized_text","source_object_id":null}]]],["display_name","Decrypt2"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--9def5213-7b43-52ba-9fec-85ebb25bfd91","120":"instance--dc80bd53-9dcf-5ff6-907e-65a49ce7a8e7","150":"instance--b58d88ad-c2eb-53c1-a24e-c8f8746b7525","180":"instance--0c42c74a-23d8-59c2-a530-2ced579a78c6","210":"instance--59b8b12a-2098-5d31-9c57-ac8d3b312429","240":"instance--e9924fb9-62fd-5537-8bdf-fc78ab373e29","270":"instance--ff96cfcf-be34-5e6a-80ef-00df35caf94a","30":"instance--c39c0d37-2e0a-5e11-9c21-e241c01bb9eb","300":"instance--1460f1b8-a43f-592c-ae34-5b86c605731d","330":"instance--e5d7aab8-c205-5970-9334-6bde91c7ffbb","60":"instance--edcf38ec-6bff-5089-84b3-51bde36c60f8","90":"instance--860c22df-3628-5756-899a-901f69fbcad7"},"id":"software","instance":"instance--d562b69c-9a04-5f30-a5ee-3888fe0b887b","properties":[["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"The Linux version of Winnti is comprised of two files: a main backdoo